How It All Works (Explanations)
​The Liquid Data Storage & Tubes (LiquidDataContainer):
​Instead of traditional solid-state silicon drives, data is suspended in a specialized optical fluid matrix (storing 12.5 Petabytes per liter).
​High-pressure magnetic transfer tubes move the fluid safely between the main core tanks and processing units without friction leaks or thermal buildup.
​The Interstellar Browser (InterstellarBrowserRelay):
​Bypasses traditional radio wave delays (which would take years across light-years) by utilizing a quantum entanglement subspace relay.
​Gives your starship crew seamless, unlimited access to Earth's internet, archives, and live media streams anywhere in the universe with near-zero latency.

